    "classification": "normal",
    "type": "social",
    "difficulty": 13,
    "notes": "<h3>Normal | Social</h3>\n<p><em>An accomplished merchant with a large operation.</em><br><strong>Motives &amp; Tactics:</strong> Abuse power, gather resources, mobilize minions</p>\n<p><strong>Difficulty:</strong> 13 | <strong>Thresholds:</strong> 5/9 | <strong>HP:</strong> 5 | <strong>Stress:</strong> 3</p>\n<p><strong>ATK:</strong> -2 | Weapon: Melee | 1d6+2 physical</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Experience:</strong> Contracts +2, Trade +2</p>\n<h4>Features</h4>\n<p><strong>The Runaround - Passive</strong>: When a PC rolls a 14 or lower on a Charm Roll made against the Merchant, they must <strong>mark a Stress</strong>.</p>\n<p><strong>Art of the Deal - Action</strong>: Spend a Fear to offer a PC a dangerous bargain for something they need - Charm Reaction Roll (17). On a failure, they must <strong>mark 2 Stress</strong> or take the deal.</p>\n<p><strong>The Best Muscle Money Can Buy - Action</strong>: Once per scene, <strong>mark a Stress</strong> to summon 1d4+1 Guards, who appear at Far range.</p>\n",
